OpenProcessor segmenter — third-party attributions
==================================================

The segmenter service in this directory wraps Meta's Segment Anything
Model 3 (SAM 3) to serve the detection cascade's segmenter leg. See
../../docs/CURATION.md and ./README.md for how it is used.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
SAM 3 (the model + Python library)
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Source:   https://github.com/facebookresearch/sam3
License:  Both the code (the sam3 Python library) and the pretrained
          weights are "SAM Materials" under Meta's SAM License (a
          custom license, not OSI-approved, not Apache-2.0):
          https://github.com/facebookresearch/sam3/blob/f1647e8d0c1d280991f4d1b7d974c2704537fe66/LICENSE
          Section 1(b)(i) requires a copy of the license with any
          distributed SAM Materials; the image carries it at
          /usr/share/licenses/sam3/LICENSE. Section 1(b)(iv) forbids
          reverse engineering and 1(b)(v) restricts trade-controlled
          use. Verify current terms at the HuggingFace model card
          (`facebook/sam3`, gated) before redistributing.
Use:      The Dockerfile pip-installs SAM 3 into the image; the service
          imports ``sam3.model_builder.build_sam3_image_model`` and
          ``sam3.model.sam3_image_processor.Sam3Processor``.

The SAM 3 weights are pulled from HuggingFace at first run. The
HuggingFace token is supplied via the ``HF_TOKEN`` environment variable
(``HUGGINGFACE_HUB_TOKEN`` and ``HUGGING_TOKEN`` are also accepted), and
is forwarded into the container by docker-compose.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
Architectural inspiration: efwfe/Labely
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Source:   https://github.com/efwfe/Labely
License:  README states "MIT License" (no LICENSE file in the repo as of
          2026-05-09; the README claim is treated as authoritative for
          attribution purposes).
Use:      The shape of this service — a FastAPI process that loads
          ``Sam3Processor`` once on startup and exposes a single
          text-prompt segmentation endpoint — was informed by reading
          ``services/sam3_inference/main.py`` in the Labely repository.
          The implementation here is a clean rewrite (no copied code):
          async-correct (inference runs in a thread executor behind a
          per-processor lock), structured logging, HuggingFace-token
          aware, and matched to this project's request/response shape
          (``POST /segment`` with ``crop_jpeg_b64`` +
          ``text_prompt`` returning crop-frame normalized bboxes).

If the Labely project later adds a LICENSE file or changes terms, the
attribution above should be updated to match.
